    'gc.unpackProgress': 'Unpacked {rows} systems into {shards} shard(s)…',
    'gc.unpackNote': 'Gzip cannot be decoded from the middle, so «Resume import» re-reads the whole archive to skip what is already written — that is hours of CPU on every restart. Unpacking does it once: the archive becomes compressed TSV shards of {count} systems, and after that resuming costs O(1) — the import simply starts from the next file. Shards can be moved one by one (rsync/scp), served as a mirror and deleted as the import proceeds (GALAXY_SHARDS_PRUNE=1). Unpacking can run while the download is still going — it reads the file as it grows.',
