    'gc.timeoutError': 'The database did not manage to write a batch in time (statement timeout): PostgREST gives each request only a few seconds. Slow batches are split in half and retried, and rows the database will not take even one by one are deferred and written at the end of the pass. You can simply resume the import from the saved point once; if the error keeps coming back it is the PostgREST ceiling, not a coincidence: give the web process a direct Postgres (SUPABASE_DB_URL, see the warning above) or run the import when the database is less busy.',
