    'gc.writeModeFallback': ' (PostgREST, slower — add SUPABASE_DB_URL for direct Postgres)',
    'gc.importNote': 'If the archive is not on disk yet, the import downloads it first (resuming after drops) and then reads it from disk; RAM < 1 GB. An interrupted import resumes: the dump is re-read from disk (the network is no longer needed), already written systems are skipped, so nothing is written to the database twice. Duplicates of one system in the dump (the same name or the same id64 in one batch) collapse into one row — otherwise Postgres aborts the upsert with «cannot affect row a second time». Batches that do not fit the database statement timeout are automatically split in half and retried. When finished, the points file is uploaded to the galaxy-data bucket (and always to the data directory, so a storage failure no longer means «no cloud»), and the «All systems» layer on the map starts working. The catalog counters below may lag by a minute — they come from a cache.',
