    'gc.postgrestTitle': 'Writes go through PostgREST — the full catalogue cannot be imported this way',
    'gc.postgrestBody': 'PostgREST writes in 200-row batches, and on the full dump (~2×10⁸ systems) the database sooner or later answers “canceling statement due to statement timeout” even for a single row — the import dies a few percent in (here it looked like “supabase upsert failed: … statement timeout (name / id64)” at 2.7%). Through PostgREST the dump takes a day; “Resume” repeats the same thing.',
    'gc.solution': 'Fix:',
    'gc.solutionBody': 'give the web process a direct Postgres URL and attach',
    'gc.solutionTail': 'to the Supabase stack docker network:',
    'gc.afterRestart': 'Both values and the network are set by deploy/start-monitoring.sh (npm run monitoring:up). After the restart press “Check DB connection” — you should see “direct Postgres (db) — connection works” and “Write mode: pg”. Already written rows are not lost: “Resume import” continues from the saved point and the archive is not re-downloaded.',
