    'gc.planCalc': 'The update plan is being computed…',
    'gc.autoTitle': 'Download and apply the smallest dump that closes the catalogue gap',
    'gc.autoButton': 'Update catalogue (auto)',
    'gc.planBody': 'The full systems.json.gz (5.9 GiB) is needed once. Spansh publishes the same catalogue as deltas — systems_1day (~4 MiB), systems_1week (~21 MiB), systems_1month (~88 MiB): same format, same upsert, so the nightly update takes seconds, not a week. A delta does not rebuild the point cloud (that is a full pass over 2×10⁸ rows) — the full import updates it.',
    'gc.segmentsBody': 'The download uses {count} parallel Range connections (GALAXY_DOWNLOAD_SEGMENTS): on a thin link this is the main way to cut 6 GiB from a week to hours. Each segment’s progress sits next to the archive and survives a restart.',
