    'gc.downloadError': 'Download: {error}',
    'gc.downloadInterrupted': 'The download was interrupted by a process restart — the bytes already fetched are in place, press “Resume download”.',
    'gc.archiveNote1': '“Download archive” takes the file named above under “What to download now” (usually a delta); “Download full dump” is always 5.9 GiB. Each variant has its own file, so the nightly delta does not overwrite the full archive that took days.',
    'gc.archiveNote2': 'The systems.json.gz dump (~6 GiB) lives in {dir} (on the server this is a separate disk mounted under the directory). Before a new dump is loaded the previous one is deleted, and after a successful import the archive itself is removed — it is no longer needed, the next update arrives as a delta. The import always reads the dump from disk: after a connection drop the download continues from the saved byte (HTTP Range), and “Resume import” re-reads the local file and skips already written systems — no need to download 6 GiB again. A corrupt archive is detected by a gzip check and downloaded again.',
